{"Local recovery-code update writes an incompatible credential payload - the helper tries updateCredential with UserCredentialModel containing a JSON array string of raw codes, but RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel expects structured RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialData and RecoveryAuthnCodesSecretData JSON blobs, causing deserialization failures during login/consumption and account-console reads": 0.8392787575721741, "Recovery-code lookup now prefers federated credentials over local storage - getCredential(UserModel) implementation scans getFederatedCredentialsStream() before getStoredCredentialsByTypeStream(), reversing the documented credential-resolution contract and causing callers to read federated values even when newer local credentials exist": 0.6173709630966187, "Federated recovery credential can mask local credential - callers using RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils.getCredential(user) may select a stale, malformed, or missing federated credential ahead of a valid local one, or cause unhandled empty Optional during login rendering/authentication": 0.7054228782653809, "Recovery-code update stores incompatible payload in federated provider - the helper passes a JSON array of raw recovery codes through UserCredentialModel.challengeResponse, but later recovery-code reads expect the structured credential/secret data format used by RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel": 0.8297531008720398, "Federated recovery codes cannot be deleted - the storage provider adds recovery-code create/read/validate support but does not expose recovery codes as disableable or remove them in disableCredentialType(), leaving federated recovery-code credentials intact during account-management or admin deletion flows": 0.9051972031593323, "Recovery-code updates and deletes only operate on stored credentials, not federated ones - the provider's createCredential() and deleteCredential() methods only interact with stored/local credentials while the new utility adds federated credential lookup, causing asymmetrical lifecycle operations where federated values may be left behind during deletion or reconfiguration": 0.4553765058517456, "supportsCredentialType can throw when the credential type is null - the new branch does credentialType.equals(RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel.TYPE) without null guard, which would crash the provider instead of returning false when callers probe support with null or partially initialized type": 0.8739424347877502}